_handle directly as send_message.to. Optional filters narrow visibility.", "input_schema": {"schema_version": "acs-mcp-list-collaborators/2", "required": ["project_id"], "optional": ["scope_handle", "name", "roles", "states", "cursor", "limit"], "json_schema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": ["project_id"], "properties": {"project_id": {"type": "string"}, "scope_handle": {"type": "string"}, "name": {"type": "string"}, "roles": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "states": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "cursor": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "limit": {"type": "integer"}}}}, "security_scopes": ["collaborators.read"]}, "send_message": {"description": "Send natural content from your authenticated identity to a collaborator. Use this tool for replies, corrections and handoffs; reply_to names original message handles. Defaults to invoke + async. sync waits for the recipient's first explicit reply, including clarification. message_only does not wake the recipient. Timeout leaves communication intact. Reuse client_request_id for the same send's retry; intentional identical sends use different IDs.", "input_schema": {"schema_version": "acs-mcp-send-message/2", "required": ["project_id", "to", "content"], "optional": ["client_request_id", "reply_to", "activation", "response_mode", "wait_timeout_seconds", "deadline"], "json_schema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": ["project_id", "to", "content"], "properties": {"project_id": {"type": "string"}, "to": {"type": "string"}, "content": {"type": "string"}, "client_request_id": {"type": "string"}, "reply_to": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "maxItems": 32}, "activation": {"type": "string", "enum": ["invoke", "message_only"], "default": "invoke"}, "response_mode": {"type": "string", "enum": ["async", "sync"], "default": "async"}, "wait_timeout_seconds": {"type": ["integer", "null"], "minimum": 0}, "deadline": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}}}, "security_scopes": ["message.send"]}, "read_message": {"description": "Read permitted original content, relationships and the first explicit Agent reply. Also accepts notification_handle to read an ACS system notification and its own Native delivery state. Reading preserves Inbox and history. The original and embedded first reply each obey max_inline_bytes; follow returned read_message actions using that body's handle and next_offset. Native output is not a reply.", "input_schema": {"schema_version": "acs-mcp-read-message/3", "required": ["project_id", "handle"], "optional": ["max_inline_bytes", "offset"], "json_schema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": ["project_id", "handle"], "properties": {"project_id": {"type": "string"}, "handle": {"type": "string", "description": "A message_handle, response_handle or notification_handle returned by ACS."}, "max_inline_bytes": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 65536, "default": 16384, "description": "Byte budget for each original and embedded reply body. Follow returned read_message continuations for either body."}, "offset": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "default": 0}}}}, "security_scopes": ["message.read"]}, "check_inbox": {"description": "List messages addressed to your authenticated identity without consuming them. Read content with read_message; reply using send_message with from as to and message_handle in reply_to. notifications lists ACS system notices: pass notification_handle to read_message. with filters peer addresses, not notification handles. next_cursor continues the page; resume_cursor discovers later messages.", "input_schema": {"schema_version": "acs-mcp-check-inbox/2", "required": ["project_id"], "optional": ["cursor", "limit", "with", "notification_cursor"], "json_schema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "required": ["project_id"], "properties": {"project_id": {"type": "string"}, "cursor": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "limit": {"type"